{"Group-based user filtering bypassed when only V2 feature flag enabled - UsersResource.searchForUser() and BruteForceUsersResource.searchForUser() call auth.groups().getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() unconditionally, but the feature-flag guard only activates under ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ (V1); when only V2 is enabled, group-based filtering is skipped entirely, allowing unauthorized access to users outside the admin's managed groups": 0.304132878780365, "Null pointer dereference in hasPermission() when resource type has no scopes - In FineGrainedAdminPermissionEvaluator.hasPermission(), lines 103-109 fetch the resourceTypeResource and attempt to get scopes without null checks. If AdminPermissionsSchema.SCHEMA.getResourceTypeResource() returns null, line 106 will throw a NullPointerException": 0.38197800517082214, "orElseThrow() call in hasPermission() will crash if the requested scope is not found, even though scopes should be defined per resource type, creating a fragile dependency on proper schema initialization": 0.025831103324890137, "GroupPermissionsV2.getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() throws UnsupportedOperationException, breaking callers in UsersResource and BruteForceUsersResource that expect a Set<String>": 0.009105196222662926, "When authz is null in GroupPermissionsV2, the null resourceStore/policyStore fields passed to FineGrainedAdminPermissionEvaluator cause NullPointerException in hasPermission()": 0.451155424118042, "UserPermissionsV2.canView(UserModel) overrides canView(UserModel) without calling canViewByGroup(), missing group-chain membership checks that the base class evaluateHierarchy() logic provides, breaking the authorization contract documented in UserPermissionEvaluator": 0.034521762281656265, "Inconsistent feature flag checking - AdminPermissions.registerListener() checks ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ (V1) while other methods check ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2, meaning group removal event handling may not be triggered in V2-only deployments and permissions may not be cleaned up on group deletion": 0.645989716053009, "Resource ID extracted without namespace validation in GroupPermissions.getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() - code assumes all resources with type 'Group' follow the naming convention 'group.resource.[ID]' without validating the prefix, potentially leaking access to groups if a resource was created with a non-standard name": 0.13111448287963867, "Missing backward compatibility for renamed method - GroupResourceTypeEvaluationTest.java uses ApiUtil.handleCreatedResponse() at multiple locations but the method was renamed to getCreatedId without preserving a deprecated wrapper, causing test compilation/runtime failures": 0.30045202374458313}